node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/
.DS_Store
.test-results.json

# Generated wholly from status.json by `npm run status`, so committing it
# stored the same information twice and rewrote 124 KB per work unit — it
# grew to the largest single path in the history. Nothing consumes it from
# the web (Pages serves docs/, and no page links here): it is a local
# dashboard. Run `npm run status` to rebuild it, or download the artifact
# CI publishes for a given run.
/status.html

# `npm run preview` output: iteration frames plus their sidecar. These are
# working artefacts of an authoring loop, not documentation assets — the
# committed screenshots are the nine under docs/, produced by `npm run
# capture`.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, this pattern matches a
# directory named `preview` at ANY depth, which silently swallows the
# preview PAGE at examples/preview/ — source that must be committed.
/preview/

# Scratch git worktrees used to isolate concurrent agents. These are real
# repositories, so an unqualified `git add -A` commits one as a gitlink and
# the next clone gets a dangling submodule reference it cannot resolve.
.claude/worktrees/
